                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "69c5a220-d343-3027-8c91-8a68080ac483",
                        "entry_id": "64d9968a-bb6b-3e9d-af3b-387db36313b1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Leaning or reclining, as the ancients did at their meals."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e927f453-5633-4319-a7a6-b5e64c29bcf4",
                                "sense_id": "69c5a220-d343-3027-8c91-8a68080ac483",
                                "text": "Together his accumbent pose and closed eyes denoted sleep, as an alternative to death, which the stiff, recumbent pose of previous effigies had embodied."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d6849ad4-6e0a-375a-b844-4409361fdb9b",
                        "entry_id": "64d9968a-bb6b-3e9d-af3b-387db36313b1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Lying against anything, as one part of a leaf against another leaf"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "30bd9b6e-a74e-434d-ae5b-5da207b3efcc",
                                "sense_id": "d6849ad4-6e0a-375a-b844-4409361fdb9b",
                                "text": "Distinguished from other genera, with accumbent cotyledons, in the same class and order, by the entire, nearly equal petals; and the dehiscent, nearly entirely pouch, of 2, 1- or many-seeded cells, a broad dissepiment (septum), and nearly flat valves."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "6e59a0f8-56b1-3e21-9515-af92d8d8ddf7",
                "word": "accumbent",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f95d5e7f-d43b-4e37-a022-eaf010871ce5",
                        "entry_id": "6e59a0f8-56b1-3e21-9515-af92d8d8ddf7",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "accumbents"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "364a97b7-31a8-39f4-8b2d-097b5ae1d038",
                        "entry_id": "6e59a0f8-56b1-3e21-9515-af92d8d8ddf7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who rests in an accumbent position, especially at table."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "62b0c5b2-6c42-4144-80ef-572bb752e347",
                                "sense_id": "364a97b7-31a8-39f4-8b2d-097b5ae1d038",
                                "text": "What a pennance must be done by every accumbent, in sitting out the passage through all these dishes; what a task the stomach must be put to in the concoction of so many mixtures."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "55d5ee5e-5124-4f82-8d6d-2dd7faa6612d",
                                "sense_id": "364a97b7-31a8-39f4-8b2d-097b5ae1d038",
                                "text": "Let us, indeed, see how the point of view has changed which was held in regard to those cultivated and glib accumbents who in former days were taken for real social workers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ad79a19-0470-4c1f-a01a-5ac7f5184761",
                                "sense_id": "364a97b7-31a8-39f4-8b2d-097b5ae1d038",
                                "text": "Said also to be fond of playing practical jokes, he was apparently in the habit of placing his dinner guests on inflated cushions, which were contrived to deflate suddenly, sending their unsuspecting accumbents sprawling under the tables."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
